<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply rose $16.9 bln in Sept 9 wk.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $16.9 bln in Sept 9 wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $16.9 billion in the September 9 week to $3,775.3 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure rose $14.1 billion to $4,767.4 billion. M-1 fell $2.0 billion to $1,059.4 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,762.7 billion versus $3.757.8 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
